# robotparts.dev part pages: the Specs tab's datasheet as one data-ui table, one row per field (data-ui,
# docs/CONTRACT.md §5). Each part page points <data-views> at this file with its own rows
# (/search/views/datasheet/<id>.json, build/site_pages.py datasheet_dataset): what the source states (nominal), what
# robotparts' measurements give (the median across units), what a board reports and what is derived, grouped by
# section in the server table's order. Click a value for every value behind it. Verdict (Zach's pick, 2026-10-27, the
# Measurements lane's M3 claim vs measured, build/measure_diag_lab.py claims_rows) sits beside a value only where it
# was measured. The template is data-ui's gim4305-datasheet gallery case; the server-rendered table stays inside
# <data-views> for readers without JavaScript. WHY units: inline and no Unit column (Zach, 2026-10-29: the unit sits
# right beside the value, compact): each value column names the row's unit (datasheet_dataset). WHY no source column
# here: every datasheet declares sourceColumn, and data-ui draws "Nominal source" after Nominal itself (its CONTRACT §36):
# one link to the page each value was read from, opened in one click; a private source as a plain label; on a value
# several sources state, a dropdown, the all-sources popover (right-click) and Manage sources (SCHEMA2.md 2.6 rule 5).
views:
  - type: table
    name: Datasheet
    order: [field, nominal, verdict, measured, board, derived, status, n]
    groupBy: { property: section }
    rowHeight: short
    units: inline
  - type: table
    name: Datasheet only
    filters: '!nominal.isEmpty()'
    order: [field, nominal]
    groupBy: { property: section }
    rowHeight: short
    units: inline
  - type: table
    name: Measured vs datasheet
    filters: '!measured.isEmpty()'
    order: [field, nominal, measured, verdict, delta, n, specimens, latest]
    groupBy: { property: section }
    rowHeight: short
    units: inline
